# TestLlm — a concrete, DETERMINISTIC llm adapter. Declares its family (llm) —
# the inverted arrow ; the family never names it. Named for its IDENTITY (a
# fixture-backed test provider), NOT its transport.
#
# The `handler` is the OUT-OF-PROCESS program the inline primary-adapter wait
# (Runtime::drain_outbound_to_quiescence) execs when the bound event fires : it
# reads the event payload on stdin (carries `prompt`), computes SHA-256 of the
# prompt, looks up the fixture file at $LLM_FIXTURES (or emits the deterministic
# lenient-miss placeholder), and writes `response_text=<completion>` to stdout,
# exit 0. The drainer (NOT the handler) dispatches the success verdict + marks
# the delivery delivered — the payment/verdict-capturing protocol, not tts's
# self-ack.
#
# TestProvider semantics mirror rust/src/runtime/llm_providers/test.rs so the
# OOP path lands the IDENTICAL completion the in-process llm_dispatcher lands
# (same SHA-256(prompt) -> same fixture).
Hecks.adapter "TestLlm" do
  family  "llm"
  handler "adapters/llm/llm-handler"
end
